  90:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jidctflt.c ****     /* Due to quantization, we will usually find that many of the input
  91:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jidctflt.c ****      * coefficients are zero, especially the AC terms.  We can exploit this
  92:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jidctflt.c ****      * by short-circuiting the IDCT calculation for any column in which all
  93:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jidctflt.c ****      * the AC terms are zero.  In that case each output is equal to the
  94:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jidctflt.c ****      * DC coefficient (with scale factor as needed).
  95:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jidctflt.c ****      * With typical images and quantization tables, half or more of the
  96:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jidctflt.c ****      * column DCT calculations can be simplified this way.
  97:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jidctflt.c ****      */
  98:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jidctflt.c ****     
